      "rationale": "Used for course and article bodies; a simple WYSIWYG rather than raw HTML/Markdown entry."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_umami",
      "label": "Self-hosted Umami analytics (shared pishtalk instance)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "One Umami instance hosts many websites, so Pishnam is registered as another website rather than getting a second analytics stack; exposed at /analytics by the host nginx."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_docker_compose_stack",
      "label": "Docker Compose full stack (Postgres, migrator, web, nginx)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The migrator is a one-off job that applies pending Prisma migrations then bootstraps the first admin, both idempotent; web waits for it to exit 0."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_github_actions_ci_cd",
      "label": "GitHub Actions CI/CD",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_db_tunnel",
      "label": "SSH tunnel to production Postgres (npm run db:tunnel)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Production Postgres is published on the server's loopback only (127.0.0.1:5433 -> localhost:5434), never 0.0.0.0, so a tunnel is the only route in; infra/db-tunnel.sh sets ExitOnForwardFailure and pre-checks the port because picking pishtalk's local port would silently leave Prisma pointed at the wrong DB."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_upload_security_checklist",
      "label": "Upload security checklist (src/lib/upload.ts)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Admin-auth-only, allowlisted types, magic-byte content verification (not filename/Content-Type), image re-encoding via jimp, random filenames, no execute permission, rate limiting, and UploadLog audit logging. Not optional hardening to add later \u2014 build it in from the first upload endpoint."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_jimp_reencoding",
      "label": "jimp image re-encoding (replaced sharp)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "sharp's prebuilt binaries need an x86-64-v2 CPU the production host doesn't have; jimp ships no WebP codec (so image/webp is not an accepted upload type), and removing sharp also turns off Next Image Optimization (images.unoptimized in next.config.ts). Uploads are capped at 2400px on the long edge instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_uploads_volume",
      "label": "Local-disk uploads Docker volume",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Files must live in a named Docker volume, never the app's writable container layer, or they'd be lost on every redeploy."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_nginx_uploads",
      "label": "nginx serves /uploads/* from shared volume; dev-only route fallback",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "src/app/uploads/[...path]/route.ts is a dev-only fallback so uploads are viewable without running the full nginx stack locally."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_production_host",
      "label": "Shared VPS production host (pishtalk, iranopen-insitu)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Nothing in this compose project may bind :80 (our nginx takes :8081 as host default_server), and images are never pulled on the server \u2014 ~1 in 5 TLS handshakes to ghcr.io complete, and 3.8 GB RAM leaves no headroom for next build, so CI builds and streams images over SSH."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_build_time_config",
      "label": "NEXT_PUBLIC_* build-time configuration",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Frozen into the bundle by next build (server-side code included), passed as Docker build args by the deploy workflow rather than read from the server's .env; pointing at a real domain means editing SITE_URL in deploy.yml and redeploying."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_rollback",
      "label": "Rollback by image retag",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Every deploy leaves an image tagged with the commit SHA; rolling back is a retag, but it rolls back code only \u2014 prisma migrate deploy has no down-migrations."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_translation_strategy",
      "label": "Parallel xFa/xEn fields vs *Translation tables",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Rich-text-heavy models (Course, Article) use a separate *Translation table so adding a locale later doesn't mean a schema migration on the parent table; simple models use parallel fields and src/lib/i18n/pick.ts (pickLocaleField)."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_messages_ui_strings",
      "label": "messages/{fa,en}.json \u2014 UI strings only",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Content always lives in the database, never in message files, so it stays admin-editable."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_ci_yml",
      "label": "ci.yml \u2014 PR and push checks",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "No E2E step: @playwright/test is installed and npm run test:e2e exists, but there is no playwright.config.ts and no specs, so the command currently fails; the CI job was removed rather than left permanently red."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_deploy_yml",
      "label": "deploy.yml \u2014 image build, SSH stream, rollout",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Builds web (and migrator only when its inputs changed), docker save, streams to the server over SSH, retags to :current, rolls the stack at /opt/pishnam, then polls /robots.txt through the published port."
    }
  ],
